{%- comment -%}
  Not a visible section — no presets, not in any group, rendered directly
  from layout/theme.liquid via `{% section 'product-card-fetch' %}` (same
  trick as sections/cart-drawer.liquid) so it always has the stable id
  "product-card-fetch" regardless of what page you're on. That stability is
  the entire point: rpl-recently-viewed.js fetches
  `/products/{handle}?section_id=product-card-fetch` to get one product's
  card as HTML, from any page, without needing to know some
  template-generated runtime section id.

  Renders nothing on a normal page load (`product` is blank there); only
  produces output when Shopify resolves it against a specific product via
  that per-handle fetch.

  Handles: the product no longer existing/being unpublished (route 404s,
  the fetch just fails — nothing to render either way).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if product != blank -%}
  <li class="rpl-reveal">
    {% render 'product-card', product: product, lazy: true %}
  </li>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.product_card_fetch.name",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "rpl-section-product-card-fetch"
}
{% endschema %}
